      "content": "Feeling like a ghost when your core passion is gone is a form of deep grief, and those feelings are incredibly real and overwhelming. When the external definition of \"self\" fades, finding a new essence is a slow, quiet process rather than an immediate fix. Please know that even when your former \"spark\" is gone, the capacity to feel—even this profound emptiness—is still a part of you. You do not have to have a grand purpose right now; survival and gentle exploration are enough for this moment.",
